# Vulnerability details

## Impact
An InProgress proposal could prevent any other proposals from executing indefinitely if it gets stuck. This could essentially lock up the governance of the party.
The severity depends on the specific use case, but I would categorize this as a high severity issue for a few reasons:
• It prevents any new proposals from executing, halting governance. This is very disruptive.
• There is no good way to recover besides the cancel() function, which itself has time delays. And cancel() may not even work if the proposal is truly stuck.
• Itblocks).
So in summary:
• Impact: High. Prevents new proposals, halts governance.
• Severity: High. Very disruptive, hard to recover from.


