## Impact
Neglecting varying token decimals in the rageQuit function could lead to significant discrepancies in the withdrawal amounts. Users may receive more or less than their fair share of assets, potentially leading to financial losses or excess distributions.

## Proof of Concept
The current implementation of the rageQuit function does not consider the decimals property of ERC-20 tokens when calculating withdrawal amounts. As ERC-20 tokens can have a wide range of decimal values, the failure to normalize token amounts to the smallest unit which is wei can result in incorrect transfer of token amounts.

